-- Age Discrimination Act 2004 (with AHRC Act 1986 ss 3, 46P, 46PH, 46PO), the older worker's questions -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_age-discrimination-act-2004_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts are from Chloe's life (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe, event c092: retires at 63 in 2066).
-- ASSUMPTION: her employer, Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd, is a trading corporation the Act reaches (s 10(8)).
-- The life says she retires by choice; the forced-retirement fixtures are counterfactuals. The other fixtures are
-- HYPOTHETICAL.

