§ `ss 6, 14-16 -- was I discriminated against on the ground of my age`

#ASSERT `How was I discriminated against` `treated worse because of my age` EQUALS `direct discrimination (s 14)`
#ASSERT `How was I discriminated against` `treated worse because of what is assumed of people my age` EQUALS `direct discrimination (s 14)`
#ASSERT `How was I discriminated against` `treated worse because of a disability, not my age` EQUALS `not discrimination on the ground of my age`
#ASSERT `How was I discriminated against` `a recent-degree requirement not shown reasonable` EQUALS `indirect discrimination (s 15)`
#ASSERT `How was I discriminated against` `a recent-degree requirement shown reasonable` EQUALS `not discrimination on the ground of my age`

#ASSERT NOT `Was I discriminated against on the ground of my age` `treated worse for my performance only`

§ `s 18 with its exemptions`

#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `Chloe told by Jarrah to retire at 63 (c092)` EQUALS `unlawful age discrimination in employment (s 18)`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `a 64-year-old removalist a court finds cannot do the lifting because of age, dismissed` EQUALS `not unlawful: I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age (s 18(4))`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `a 64-year-old applicant a court finds cannot do the lifting because of age, not hired` EQUALS `not unlawful: I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age (s 18(4))`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `a 64-year-old denied training, though a court finds the lifting beyond him` EQUALS `unlawful age discrimination in employment (s 18)`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `a 19-year-old paid a junior rate` EQUALS `not unlawful: youth wages (s 25)`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `a 45-year-old kept out of an over-55s retraining scheme` EQUALS `not unlawful: positive discrimination (s 33)`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `dismissed at 65 under an enterprise agreement term` EQUALS `not unlawful: direct compliance with a law, order or instrument (ss 38-40)`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `dismissed by an employer the Act does not reach` EQUALS `outside the reach of the Act (s 10)`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `a recent-degree requirement for promotion` EQUALS `unlawful age discrimination in employment (s 18)`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `the same requirement shown reasonable` EQUALS `not discrimination on the ground of my age (ss 14-16)`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `not hired as live-in housekeeper because of age` EQUALS `not unlawful: a domestic job in the employer's home (s 18(3))`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `dismissed as live-in housekeeper because of age` EQUALS `unlawful age discrimination in employment (s 18)`

§ `s 18(2)(c) -- can I be made to retire at an age`

#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire at an age` `Chloe retiring at 63 by choice (c092)` EQUALS `nobody is making me: retiring by choice is not discrimination`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire at an age` `Chloe required by Jarrah to retire at 63 (c092)` EQUALS `no: making me retire because of my age is unlawful dismissal on the ground of age (s 18(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire at an age` `required to retire, a court finding the job beyond me because of age` EQUALS `yes: I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age (s 18(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire at an age` `required to retire by an enterprise agreement term` EQUALS `yes: in direct compliance with a law, order or instrument (ss 38-40)`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire at an age` `required to retire by an employer the Act does not reach` EQUALS `not under this Act: it does not reach my employer (s 10)`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire at an age` `required to retire under a Commission exemption` EQUALS `yes: under a Commission exemption (s 47)`

